        "q": "L1 vs L2 regularization geometrically. Why L1 sparse, L2 not?",
        "tracks": [],
        "subcategory": "machine_learning",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "level": "senior_ds",
        "domain": "general",
        "a": "L2 (Ridge): penalty=Σβ². Minimize Loss+λΣβ². Constraint β₁²+β₂²≤r (circle). Tangent point interior (not on axis)→non-zero β. L1 (Lasso): penalty=Σ|β|. Constraint |β₁|+|β₂|≤r (diamond). Diamond has sharp corners at axes. Tangent often on axis (β₂=0)→sparse. Why: (1) Diamond points outward on axes. (2) Loss contours elliptical (gradient inward). (3) If contour tangent hits corner, solution there (β=0). (4) Circle smooth-contours never hit axis exactly. L2 shrinks all toward zero (ball), L1 shrinks some exactly to zero (diamond corners). Example: loss minimum at (1,1). With L2 λ=0.5: min around (0.7,0.7) (both non-zero). With L1 λ=0.5: min near (0.5,0) (one zero, sparse). Higher λ→more zeros (L1), more shrinkage (L2). L1 removes weak features, L2 keeps all (small). When use: L1 when features redundant (eliminate), L2 when all matter (shrink equally). Elastic Net combines both."
