        "domain": "fintech",
        "a": "import ruptures as rpt; algo=rpt.Pelt(model='l2').fit(data); breakpoints=algo.predict(pen=10). PELT: efficient, finds optimal breakpoints minimizing cost with penalty for too many changes. Change point vs anomaly: (1) Change point-permanent level shift (revenue $10K→$8K/day, stays). Anomaly-temporary spike. (2) Scope-change point affects forecast. Anomaly doesn't. (3) Detection-change points via piecewise linear. Anomalies via deviation. Example: revenue $10K±$500 normally. Day 50: dips to $7K, stays. Change point. Day 51-60: stays $7K (anomaly detector ignores, change point detector sees shift). Use: (1) Change points-product launch, pricing change, seasonal shift. (2) Anomalies-data errors, one-off events. Real: detect post-update revenue drop (bad feature), adjust forecast. PELT finds when, anomaly detection only flags outlier."
